  "casts": [
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c301",
      "authorFid": 1000001,
      "minutesAgo": 720,
      "text": "The stablecoin settlement stack is quietly consolidating. Three of the top five issuers now clear through the same two prime brokers, and nobody seems to think this is a problem.\n\nFor anyone who watched the 2008 tri-party repo unwind up close: this is that, with fewer adults in the room.",
      "replies": 6,
      "likes": 1312,
      "recasts": 54,
      "views": 18400,
      "embeds": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "quote": {
            "hash": "0xq1000001",
            "authorFid": 1000003,
            "minutesAgo": 4320,
            "text": "In 1781 terms this is the insurance chapter, not the shipping chapter. We traced Q2 cross-domain arb flow: over 60% routed through three builders.\n\nThe Auction and the Aqueduct, our new piece with…",
            "embeds": [
              {
                "type": "image",
                "url": "https://picsum.photos/seed/aqueduct/1200/675"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c302",
      "authorFid": 1000007,
      "minutesAgo": 840,
      "text": "the committee meeting where they decided every chart in every deck must go up and to the right",
      "replies": 41,
      "likes": 3921,
      "recasts": 402,
      "views": 220100,
      "embeds": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "url": "https://picsum.photos/seed/danafilm/1200/675"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c303",
      "authorFid": 1000008,
      "minutesAgo": 780,
      "text": "I saw this article all over the timeline today and thought the big lab wrote an explainer on x402. how crazy! so i gave it a read\n\nwrong expectation. this is not them shilling x402.\n\nwhat it actually is: a jupyter notebook walkthrough showing how to build a controlled spending layer around agent payments, with the protocol as the settlement rail. the interesting part is the budget attestation loop, which nobody is talking about",
      "replies": 2,
      "likes": 16,
      "recasts": 1,
      "views": 1500,
      "embeds": [
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "quote": {
            "hash": "0xq1000002",
            "authorFid": 1000010,
            "minutesAgo": 2880,
            "text": "Great x402 blog this week!\n\nThe post leans into the x402 payment flow via the AgentCore Payment implementation. Check it out!!",
            "embeds": []
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c304",
      "authorFid": 1000009,
      "minutesAgo": 600,
      "recastedByFid": 1000004,
      "text": "A full deep dive on this exact subject if you are interested",
      "replies": 3,
      "likes": 187,
      "recasts": 22,
      "views": 29500,
      "embeds": [
        {
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://themeter.xyz/mandate",
          "domain": "themeter.xyz",
          "title": "The Meter and the Mandate",
          "description": "Why the payments giant wants both an inference router and a wallet network. The same company, built twice. The first time, the inventory was NFTs.",
          "image": "https://picsum.photos/seed/meterarticle/1200/675",
          "article": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c305",
      "authorFid": 1000005,
      "minutesAgo": 300,
      "threadCount": 3,
      "text": "1/ Everyone is pricing the rate cut. Nobody is pricing the collateral migration that follows it.\n\nA thread on what happens to onchain money markets when T-bill yield stops being the risk-free benchmark:",
      "replies": 18,
      "likes": 892,
      "recasts": 143,
      "views": 96200,
      "embeds": []
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c306",
      "authorFid": 1000013,
      "minutesAgo": 240,
      "text": "Daily: DEX/CEX spot ratio printed 31%, a new high.\n\nThe interesting part is WHERE it came from. Not majors. Long-tail pairs that simply do not exist on centralized venues anymore. The listings pipeline moved onchain and nobody sent a press release.",
      "replies": 12,
      "likes": 640,
      "recasts": 88,
      "views": 51900,
      "embeds": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "url": "https://picsum.photos/seed/dexdata/1200/675"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c307",
      "authorFid": 1000014,
      "minutesAgo": 180,
      "text": "intern got yelled at for saying the quiet part: most \"institutional adoption\" announcements are a custody agreement and a blog post",
      "replies": 27,
      "likes": 2210,
      "recasts": 310,
      "views": 187000,
      "embeds": []
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c308",
      "authorFid": 1000002,
      "minutesAgo": 1140,
      "text": "Every successful marketplace has winners and losers.\n\nBut some participants make it more of a dark forest than a cheerful bazaar. We find some direct evidence for this — and some simple math that predicts who defects first.",
      "replies": 9,
      "likes": 421,
      "recasts": 67,
      "views": 40300,
      "embeds": [
        {
          "type": "link",
          "url": "https://openrouter.example/caching-cheaters",
          "domain": "researchhub.xyz",
          "title": "Caching Cheaters on OpenRouter",
          "description": "The full essay — with a more philosophical market-structure frame, the economics of open source, and the complete analysis and appendices referenced — can be found here.",
          "image": "https://picsum.photos/seed/cachingcheat/1200/675",
          "article": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c309",
      "authorFid": 1000012,
      "minutesAgo": 1080,
      "text": "MiCA enforcement update: the first fine finally landed and it is... €40k. For a firm doing €2B annual volume.\n\nCompliance departments across the continent breathing out simultaneously",
      "replies": 5,
      "likes": 233,
      "recasts": 19,
      "views": 21700,
      "embeds": []
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xa1b2c310",
      "authorFid": 1000006,
      "minutesAgo": 90,
      "text": "ok the agent payments demos are getting good. watched one negotiate a bulk API discount, split settlement across two chains, and file the receipt into accounting. 40 seconds end to end.\n\nthe boring plumbing era was the whole point",
      "replies": 14,
      "likes": 505,
