      "hash": "0xself0001",
      "authorFid": 9152,
      "minutesAgo": 4560,
      "text": "I understand the pushback against Claude watermarks, but it's more product gap/short term nuisance than a real issue.\n\nThe end state is a provenance layer with hashes of your content & prompts, attesting that your input predates Claude's and makes up X% of the output.\n\nBasically a receipts system for authorship. The models get good enough that \"did a human write this\" becomes the wrong question, and \"which human commissioned it\" becomes the right one.",
      "replies": 1,
      "likes": 7,
      "recasts": 0,
      "views": 667,
      "embeds": [],
      "truncate": true,
      "viewerLiked": true
    },
    {
      "hash": "0xself0002",
      "authorFid": 9152,
      "minutesAgo": 5760,
      "text": "Can't remember the last time a new L1/L2 was announced. Do we finally have enough chains?",
